{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-005", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh, Netherlands to boost green maritime & logistics ties", "content": "Bangladesh and the Netherlands are strengthening maritime and logistics cooperation with focus on sustainable transport, port connectivity, shipbuilding, ship recycling and inland waterways. \nBIDA’s proposed smart and green logistics corridors aim to link economic zones, ports and industrial hubs through greener, technology-led infrastructure.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-netherlands-to-boost-green-maritime-logistics-ties-310255-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-006", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s apparel sourcing window reopens—for now", "content": "India’s US tariff window is open but closing fast.\nAfter cumulative duties hit 50 per cent in late 2025, the February 6, 2026 interim deal cut India to 18 per cent, below Vietnam (20%), Bangladesh (19%) and Indonesia (19%).\nBut the 10 per cent Section 122 surcharge expires on July 24, 2026.\nH2 2025 imports collapsed 25.4 per cent to $2.216 billion; AEPC now eyes a $16 billion FY27.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-apparel-sourcing-window-reopens-for-now-310254-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-007", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "expand", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India’s RSWM swings to FY26 profit; EBITDA more than doubles", "content": "RSWM Limited has returned to profitability in FY26, reporting EBITDA of ₹327 crore (~$34.37 million) and PAT of ₹52 crore (~$5.46 million) against a loss last year. \nThe company is expanding into recycled PET through acquisition of LNJ GreenPET and investing ₹92 crore (~$9.63 million) to enhance knitted fabric capacity. \nRSWM said the initiatives align with sustainability goals, and value-added growth. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-rswm-swings-to-fy26-profit-ebitda-more-than-doubles-310250-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-008", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-Nigeria textile trade yet to reach full potential: Indian envoy", "content": "Despite longstanding economic ties between India and Nigeria, bilateral textile trade has not reached its full potential, Indian high commissioner to Nigeria Abhishek Singh recently said.\nThe former is ready to support the latter’s textile revival agenda through investments across the value chain.\nIndia is exploring collaboration between its NIFT and the Nigerian Fashion Institute in Lagos, he added.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-nigeria-textile-trade-yet-to-reach-full-potential-indian-envoy-310244-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-009", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam, Sri Lanka to boost logistics, textiles cooperation", "content": "Vietnam and Sri Lanka should prioritise logistics connectivity and cargo trans-shipment cooperation, an area that matches Sri Lanka’s advantages and Vietnam’s demand to expand its reach into the Indian Ocean, Vietnamese President To Lam has said. \nHe also called for stronger cooperation in highly complementary sectors like textiles and garments which could be implemented quickly and produce clear results. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-sri-lanka-to-boost-logistics-textiles-cooperation-310243-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-010", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rules of origin under regulations issued for Vietnam-UAE CEPA", "content": "To implement the Vietnam-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA), Vietnam’s Ministry of Industry and Trade recently issued a circular stipulating rules of origin for goods under the pact.\nThe document took effect on May 5, 2026.\nThe circular sets out the scope of regulation, applicable entities and principles for determining the origin of goods under the CEPA.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/rules-of-origin-under-regulations-issued-for-vietnam-uae-cepa-310241-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-011", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh BGMEA, Germany’s GIZ sign MoU for green RMG transformation", "content": "Bangladesh trade body BGMEA and Germany’s GIZ recently signed an MoU to strengthen sustainability, energy efficiency and circularity in Bangladesh’s RMG industry. \nThe MoU will remain effective from May 2026 to February 2028. \nThe cooperation is designed to align industrial growth with international sustainability benchmarks and climate commitments. \nA major focus is energy transition of the sector. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-bgmea-germany-s-giz-sign-mou-for-green-rmg-transformation-310253-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-012", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh passed China but missed the US sourcing shift", "content": "Bangladesh has overtaken China in US apparel supplies, but mainly because China’s shipments collapsed faster.\nOTEXA data show Bangladesh’s US exports fell 8.38 per cent, while Vietnam and Cambodia gained share.\nTexPro indicates Bangladesh remains woven-heavy, limiting its ability to capture China’s MMF-led shift.\nFuture gains depend on fibre diversification, speed and value-added capability.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-passed-china-but-missed-the-us-sourcing-shift-310252-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-12-013", "date": "2026-05-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Bangladesh RMG sector to adopt blockchain-based transparency & DPP", "content": "Bangladesh’s readymade garment (RMG) sector is set to adopt blockchain-based transparency and Digital Product Passport (DPP) systems ahead of the European Union’s 2027 regulations. \nBGMEA and Dutch traceability platform AWARE signed an MoU to enable end-to-end traceability of fibres, yarns, and garments through blockchain-backed digital records, helping exporters strengthen compliance.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-rmg-sector-to-adopt-blockchain-based-transparency-dpp-310229-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
